---
import CalculatorLayout from '@layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import FatIntakeCalculator from '@components/islands/FatIntakeCalculator.astro';
import { getCalculator } from '@data/calculators';
const calc = getCalculator('health', 'fat-intake-calculator')!;
const faqs = [
  { question: 'How much fat should I eat per day?', answer: 'Health authorities recommend that 20–35% of your daily calories come from fat. On a 2,000-calorie diet, that is roughly 44–78 grams of fat per day, since each gram of fat provides 9 calories.' },
  { question: 'How do I calculate my fat intake in grams?', answer: 'Multiply your daily calories by the fat percentage, then divide by 9 (the calories in a gram of fat). For 2,000 calories at 30%: 2,000 × 0.30 = 600 calories from fat, ÷ 9 ≈ 67 grams a day.' },
  { question: 'Is dietary fat bad for you?', answer: 'No — fat is essential for hormones, vitamin absorption and cell health. What matters is the type: favour unsaturated fats and limit saturated and trans fats.' },
  { question: 'What is the difference between healthy and unhealthy fats?', answer: 'Unsaturated fats (olive and avocado oil, nuts, seeds, oily fish) support heart health and should make up most of your intake. Saturated fats (fatty meat, butter, full-fat dairy) are best kept moderate, and artificial trans fats are best avoided entirely.' },
  { question: 'How do I know my calorie target?', answer: 'Estimate your daily calorie needs with the calorie calculator, then enter that number here to get your fat range.' },
];
---
<CalculatorLayout calculator={calc} reviewedOn="2026-07-18" intro="Find your recommended daily fat intake in grams, based on your calorie target and the standard 20–35% of calories from fat." faqs={faqs}>
  <FatIntakeCalculator />
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <h2>How the range is calculated</h2>
    <p>The Acceptable Macronutrient Distribution Range puts fat at 20–35% of daily calories. Because fat provides 9 calories per gram, the calculator converts your calorie target into a gram range. Enter the calories from the <a href="/health/calorie-calculator">calorie calculator</a> for a personalised figure.</p>

    <h2>A worked example</h2>
    <p>On a 2,000-calorie diet at the mid-point of 30%: 2,000 × 0.30 = 600 calories from fat, and 600 ÷ 9 ≈ <strong>67 grams a day</strong>. The full 20–35% range works out to roughly <strong>44–78 grams</strong>, leaving room to place fat higher or lower depending on your carbohydrate and protein goals.</p>

    <h2>Quality over quantity</h2>
    <p>Within your range, prioritise unsaturated fats — olive and avocado oil, nuts, seeds and oily fish — which support heart health. Keep saturated fat moderate and avoid trans fats. Pair this with your <a href="/health/protein-calculator">protein target</a> for a balanced plan.</p>
    <p>This is general educational information, not medical or dietary advice.</p>
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>
